meta {
  name: 51 Sample Search (Search Sample popup)
  type: http
  seq: 51
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/sample-search?barcode={{sampleBarcode}}&menu=IN_HOUSE
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  barcode: {{sampleBarcode}}
  menu: IN_HOUSE
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("found or not found (never an error for an unknown barcode)", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
    expect(res.getBody().data).to.have.property("found");
  });
}

docs {
  Sample Search popup (In-House, Internal Referral and External Referral Orders).
  Find a barcode and get its sample details with the actions its status allows.

  **Query**
  - `barcode` (required, max 50): exact match, ignoring case; surrounding spaces are removed.
  - `menu` (required): `IN_HOUSE` | `INTERNAL` | `EXTERNAL`.

  **Where each menu looks** (page filters and status tabs are ignored)
  - `IN_HOUSE`: samples held by the caller's active branch (department scope applied).
  - `INTERNAL`: transfers coming TO the caller's branch (an In-Transit transfer with no logistics type
    yet stays hidden, as in the list).
  - `EXTERNAL`: transfers going FROM the caller's branch to a partner lab.

  **Response (`data`)**
  - Not found: `{ found: false, menu, barcode, foundIn: [...] }` — `foundIn` lists the other menus
    (`IN_HOUSE`, `INTERNAL`, `EXTERNAL`, `OUTSOURCE`) that do have the barcode.
  - Found: `{ found: true, menu, barcode, order, fields, sections }`.
    - `order`: `id`, `orderCode`, `externalOrderId`, `branchId`, `billingVisible` (true only when the order
      was registered at the caller's own branch). The screen loads patient / referral / billing / notes
      with `GET /orders/:id`.
    - `fields`: `processingBranch` (Internal Referral only), `originBranch` (In-House: the RM Branch; referral menus: the sending branch), `outsourceCenter`, `externalPartner` and the dates
      `sent` / `forwarded` / `outsourced` (`{ date, time }`).
    - `sections`: one per status within the barcode (usually one). Each has `kind` (`SAMPLE` or
      `TRANSFER`), `status`, `sampleType`, `container`, `sampleIds`, `transferIds`, `rows` (one test per
      row: `testName`, `department`, `category`, `subcategory`, `reportStatus`, `itemRemoved`, `routing` (see below), and in a Discarded
      / Returned section `recoverable` / `returnedVerified` of THAT row), `actions`
      (the buttons to show, already narrowed by what the server allows), `hiddenActionReasons`
      (why Store / Return / Retrieve is missing), `flags` (`recoverable` for Discarded,
      `returnedVerified` for Returned: true only when EVERY row has it; `mixed` is true when the rows differ, then
      read the rows) and `orderCancelled`.

  **`routing` of each row** (the "Send / Forward / Outsource Details" column): `{ kind, to, when: { date, time } }`.
  - `IN_HOUSE` menu follows the sample's CURRENT status: `SEND` (status Sent, `to` = destination branch), `FORWARD`
    (Forwarded, `to` = partner business) or `OUTSOURCE` (Outsourced, `to` = outsource center) with the hand-off's send
    date / time; every other status is `IN_HOUSE` with no destination, even when an older hand-off still exists (a Retrieve
    or Repeat brought the sample back), so an old destination is never shown.
  - `INTERNAL` menu: `INTERNAL_REFERRAL`, `to` = the receiving branch of the row's transfer. `EXTERNAL` menu:
    `EXTERNAL_REFERRAL`, `to` = the partner name. Both carry the transfer's send date / time.
  - `to` is `null` when none was assigned. The page-level `fields` stay for older clients.

  **Buttons.** In-House follows the requirements table per sample status; Internal / External Referral
  follow the transfer status. Store and Return on an Accepted sample appear only when every test on its
  barcode is Published. A button the server would always refuse for the report's state is left out and its
  reason is in `hiddenActionReasons`: Repeat when a result is validated (Result Done, Approved, Published),
  Send / Forward / Outsource when a report was worked on (results, notes, attachments, or past Pending),
  Retrieve when it would take the sample back to before acceptance (or recall it from another branch /
  partner) while a report is past Pending. A section with several samples keeps the button while any of
  its samples would still be accepted (group actions skip the invalid ones). For a department-scoped
  user the Store / Return reason says when the unpublished test is in a department they cannot see. Retrieve on a Discarded sample needs the recoverable flag, on a Returned sample
  the verified flag; the extra buttons `Mark Recoverable`, `Mark Not Recoverable` and
  `Mark Returned & Verified` run `bulk/set-recoverable` and `bulk/mark-returned-verified`. Users'
  permissions are applied by the screen.

  **A section whose rows carry different flags** (one barcode shared by tests of several departments, each discarded or
  returned on its own): each button stays while it can act on some row. Retrieve stays while any row qualifies (the
  recoverable / verified ones; the server retrieves those and skips the rest with the reason), `Mark Recoverable` while
  any row is not recoverable, `Mark Not Recoverable` while any row is recoverable, `Mark Returned & Verified` while any
  row is unverified. The screen sends only the rows a button can change and lists them in a confirmation first.

  **Internal Referral, a Repeat / Reject the sender already acted on.** Once the sending branch has confirmed the
  receiver's Repeat or flagged the rejected sample as Error (the sender's sample left "Sent"), the transfer section no
  longer offers Retrieve; the reason is in `hiddenActionReasons`.

  **A barcode a Repeat took off.** A Repeat takes the barcode off the sample on purpose (the tube is replaced; Collect
  makes the new barcode) and remembers it (`barcodeBeforeRepeat`). So scanning the OLD tube still works:
  - While the sample waits for its new tube (no barcode yet) the search finds it. It appears as its own section
    (`Repeat`, or `Hold` / `Cancelled` if it was held or cancelled after the Repeat) with `barcodeTakenOff` set to the
    scanned barcode and the document's Repeat buttons. Samples of the same tube that still carry the barcode appear in
    their own sections next to it (a shared tube with one test repeated shows ALL its tests). In Internal Referral the
    transfer of such a sample is found the same way.
  - A sample that carries the barcode always wins: waiting samples of another order never replace it.
  - Once the sample has a new barcode the old one is NOT found; the not-found answer carries `replacedBy` with the
    new barcode (message only, never the sample).
  Samples that never had a barcode (New, or Hold from New) cannot be found by this search.

  **Matching.** The barcode matches exactly and ignores capitals. A code with an underscore (a legal separator) is matched
  with plain equality (exact capitals) because `_` and `%` are wildcards in a case-insensitive database match.

  **Errors.** `400 VALIDATION_ERROR` when `barcode` is empty, longer than 50 characters, contains a control character
  (NUL, tab inside, newline inside ...), a `%` or a `\`, or `menu` is not one of the three values.
  `400 ACTIVE_BRANCH_REQUIRED` when the profile has no active branch (for example the business admin).
}
